# Baseline line-ending policy. Part of the _baseline kit; see
# https://github.com/Joe-User/engineering-standards -> standards/CONVENTIONS.md
#
# Normalize to LF in the repository. Without this, Windows checkouts commit CRLF
# and Linux CI runners see spurious whole-file diffs.
#
# NOTE: adding this file does not rewrite existing files. To normalize an
# existing repo, run `git add --renormalize .` as a deliberate, separate commit
# on a clean working tree, never mixed with other changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells keep CRLF. Batch files in particular can misbehave with LF
# around labels and goto.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary, so git never attempts EOL conversion or a text diff.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.bin  binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.FCStd binary

# --- repo-specific ---
# Deployed to a Raspberry Pi. LF is functionally required for systemd units and
# shell scripts, so pin them explicitly rather than relying on text=auto detection.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
